    "created_at": "2016-11-03T09:09:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-03T09:09:16Z",
    "body": "For this to be equivalent to the `dl` change, you would only be allowed to have a `div` wrapping each individual list item. Which is pointless, and you could as well have the `div` inside `li`.\n\nIf you want to group several list items together, that seems like a separate use case from that of `dl`, and I don't see why it wouldn't apply to `dl` equally.\n\nIn your examples, it seems to me it's actually two lists, so should be two `ul` elements.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
