    "created_at": "2016-11-03T17:26:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-03T17:26:27Z",
    "body": "Maybe. `div`’s content model inside `dl` could still be changed from `dt+ dd+` to `(dt+ dd+)+`, but then it wouldn’t exactly match the implicit grouping anymore. I’m not sure that’s a bad thing.\n\nThe equivalent to `<dt> Foo <dd> Bar` in Lateχ is `\\item[Foo] Bar`, whereas `<li> Baz` would be `\\item Baz`. That shows it’s a matter of philosophy whether `li` is equivalent to `dd` or `dt dd`.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
