    "created_at": "2017-09-09T14:40:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-09T14:42:33Z",
    "body": "Introducing div as a semantic groupening element without being semantic to dt/dd was an error already, but at least there was a use case that wasn't sufficiently fulfilled (think like if <tr> or <thead> where missing from the table tags) - this here, as explained can easily and logically be done by sub groups. No need to create more mess; deriving the mental model actually shows that dt/dd should have been done the non-lazy-way by adding a dgroup tag. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
